      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The step says that because the canonical quotient of Z_n(C) by B_n(C) is H_n(C), it is “not B_n(C).” The cited homology definition establishes that particular cokernel only; it does not exclude a different epimorphism Z_n(C) → B_n(C). Thus it does not refute the stated existential quotient claim. A valid witness is the complex Z → Q → 0 in Ab, with inclusion in degrees 1 to 0: Z_0=Q and B_0=Z, while every homomorphism Q → Z is zero, so B_0 is not a quotient of Z_0.",
